mapping "V5513.1" source="V5513" target="214640008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V5513 (Swedish) = SNOMED CT 214640008. Clinically: a passenger in a light truck
        (pick-up/van) hit by a train, off-public-road, during another occupation. The base ICD-10 V55.1
        has an Athena edge to SNOMED CT 437738. Target / 214640008 = (standard_concept=S, valid). It fully
        subsumes the source: every V5513 event is a motor vehicle accident off public road. The target
        drops the Swedish-only activity dimension (sport/leisure/work/etc.) and the train-collision
        specificity, but those are administrative/contextual axes, not a different clinical accident.
        Mapping type broader (target subsumes source). Confidence : Athena-verified crosswalk on the
        base V55.1, one-level-broader due to the dropped activity/counterpart dimensions.
        """
}
